\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The \textsc  {HealOps}{} seven-layer cloud architecture. Layers L1 (Container Runtime) through L7 (User \& API Gateway) form a strict dependency hierarchy. Bidirectional arrows between adjacent layers represent the Kubernetes API, Prometheus HTTP API, and gRPC channels through which the six agents exchange telemetry observations, diagnostic queries, and remediation commands. All agent-to-infrastructure interactions are mediated through the Layer~5 ToolRouter, which enforces PolicyGuard constraints before forwarding any mutating command to Layer~4.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{4}{The \HealOps {} seven-layer cloud architecture. Layers L1 (Container Runtime) through L7 (User \& API Gateway) form a strict dependency hierarchy. Bidirectional arrows between adjacent layers represent the Kubernetes API, Prometheus HTTP API, and gRPC channels through which the six agents exchange telemetry observations, diagnostic queries, and remediation commands. All agent-to-infrastructure interactions are mediated through the Layer~5 ToolRouter, which enforces PolicyGuard constraints before forwarding any mutating command to Layer~4}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces HealOps cognitive agent state-machine. Solid arrows represent the happy-path healing flow. The RETRY branch returns to ActionAgent for up to three attempts before EscalationAgent is activated. The PolicyGuard block path bypasses all retry attempts and escalates immediately.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:statemachine}{{2}{5}{HealOps cognitive agent state-machine. Solid arrows represent the happy-path healing flow. The RETRY branch returns to ActionAgent for up to three attempts before EscalationAgent is activated. The PolicyGuard block path bypasses all retry attempts and escalates immediately}{figure.2}{}}
