\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces MTTR distributions across the four fault scenarios plotted on a log scale. Notched box-plots display the median, IQR, Tukey whiskers at $1.5\!\times $\,IQR, and individual outliers as dots. \textbf  {HO} = \textsc  {HealOps}{} (blue); \textbf  {Heur} = Heuristic Script (salmon); \textbf  {K8s} = Native Kubernetes (red). Note the y-axis is independently scaled per scenario to maximize within-scenario resolution. \textsc  {HealOps}{} achieves complete stochastic dominance across all four scenarios; not a single \textsc  {HealOps}{} trial overlaps with the Native Kubernetes distribution.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mttr}{{3}{8}{MTTR distributions across the four fault scenarios plotted on a log scale. Notched box-plots display the median, IQR, Tukey whiskers at $1.5\!\times $\,IQR, and individual outliers as dots. \textbf {HO} = \HealOps {} (blue); \textbf {Heur} = Heuristic Script (salmon); \textbf {K8s} = Native Kubernetes (red). Note the y-axis is independently scaled per scenario to maximize within-scenario resolution. \HealOps {} achieves complete stochastic dominance across all four scenarios; not a single \HealOps {} trial overlaps with the Native Kubernetes distribution}{figure.3}{}}
