\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cliff's $\delta $ effect sizes with 95\% bootstrap confidence intervals (2{,}000 bootstrap iterations). Negative $\delta $ indicates \textsc  {HealOps}{} is faster. All point estimates cluster at $\delta = -1.00$, indicating complete stochastic dominance. Error bars are narrow ($<0.02$ width), confirming that the dominance is stable across bootstrap samples.}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cliffs}{{4}{9}{Cliff's $\delta $ effect sizes with 95\% bootstrap confidence intervals (2{,}000 bootstrap iterations). Negative $\delta $ indicates \HealOps {} is faster. All point estimates cluster at $\delta = -1.00$, indicating complete stochastic dominance. Error bars are narrow ($<0.02$ width), confirming that the dominance is stable across bootstrap samples}{figure.4}{}}
